{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "author-images/a-reference-a-path-reader-could-follow-is-refused",
  "title": "A reference a path reader could follow is refused when its content is built, in every spelling a reader decodes or trims: a '..' segment percent-encoded once or more, padded with whitespace or ended by '?' or '#', a backslash raw or encoded, a control character raw or encoded, an escape left after three decodings, a rest that starts once decoded with '~', a drive letter or a slash only decoding writes; a link, a data URI and an ordinary reference holding dots, an encoded dot or slash, a space, an escape that is no UTF-8, three nested encodings, an empty authority (///), a tilde or a colon further on, or a mixed-case scheme stay accepted",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4"
  ],
  "notes": "Python's MediaContent._validate_url (roomkit._media_url.is_safe_reference) and roomkit-rs's model::media_url: the rest after the scheme's :// is percent-decoded until it no longer changes, three times at most, a byte sequence that is no UTF-8 reading as U+FFFD; one a fourth decoding would still change is refused, and so is one where a backslash, a control character (Unicode Cc) or a segment, between /, ? and #, that is .. once trimmed of Unicode White_Space is left, or when the decoded rest starts with ~, a letter and a colon, or a / the raw rest does not start with. A link and a data URI are not read this way. A refused content takes no index: the first accepted event is index 0.",
